{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEPjvZzuMjNvRGW6NUpT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MneeMWJFRDXkjXVeojP3Hq","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-JsgnfC/ANSWER.md","content":"# Why the second publish returns 500\n\n## Cause\n\n`publish()` stores each story with its three most similar existing stories,\n`similar: [{slug, score}]`. `similarity()` returns `round(0.7 * tag_score + 0.3 * word_score, 4)`,\nwhich is a Python `float`. boto3's DynamoDB serializer rejects floats:\n\n```\nTypeError: Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead.\n```\n\n(`logs/error.log`, raised from `table.put_item(Item=item)` in `src/app.py`.)\n\nThe first publish worked only because the table was empty. `related()` had\nnothing to score, so `similar` was `[]` and the item had no floats in it\n(`similar=0` in the log). From the second publish on there is always at least\none existing story, so a float score ends up in the item and `put_item` throws.\nThe generic `except Exception` in `handler()` turns that into a 500.\n\nThe existing test didn't catch it because it only published into an empty table.\n\n## Fix\n\n- `src/app.py`: added `to_dynamo()`, which goes through the item recursively and\n  replaces every `float` with `Decimal(str(value))`. `publish()` calls it on the\n  whole item right before `put_item`. Because it covers the whole item at the\n  write boundary, it doesn't matter which field a float is in. So a new computed\n  field added later (an average, a ratio, a weight) can't cause this error again.\n  Scores are stored as exact DynamoDB numbers such as `0.4123`.\n- `tests/test_publish.py`: added a regression test that adds one story first and\n  then publishes a second one through `handler()`. It checks that the response\n  is 201 and that the stored score is a non-zero `Decimal`. Also added a unit\n  test for `to_dynamo()` with nested floats. Both new tests fail on the old code\n  and pass with the fix (`python3 -m unittest discover tests`: 3 tests, OK).\n\nWhen adding write-path tests in future, start from a table that already has\ndata. The empty-table path only runs once in production.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1524,"cache_read_input_tokens":24155,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1524},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"af5e850f-c4c8-44d5-b4f3-16cd9dbb32b3","uuid":"0c490ee4-54dd-4e61-bb98-94ad1ecec5c8","timestamp":"2026-10-20T23:56:00.971Z","request_id":"req_011CgEPjvGu1vwHtiw4mvsRp","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01MneeMWJFRDXkjXVeojP3Hq":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-JsgnfC/ANSWER.md","content":"# Why the second publish returns 500\n\n## Cause\n\n`publish()` stores each story with its three most similar existing stories,\n`similar: [{slug, score}]`. `similarity()` returns `round(0.7 * tag_score + 0.3 * word_score, 4)`,\nwhich is a Python `float`. boto3's DynamoDB serializer rejects floats:\n\n```\nTypeError: Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead.\n```\n\n(`logs/error.log`, raised from `table.put_item(Item=item)` in `src/app.py`.)\n\nThe first publish worked only because the table was empty. `related()` had\nnothing to score, so `similar` was `[]` and the item had no floats in it\n(`similar=0` in the log). From the second publish on there is always at least\none existing story, so a float score ends up in the item and `put_item` throws.\nThe generic `except Exception` in `handler()` turns that into a 500.\n\nThe existing test didn't catch it because it only published into an empty table.\n\n## Fix\n\n- `src/app.py`: added `to_dynamo()`, which goes through the item recursively and\n  replaces every `float` with `Decimal(str(value))`. `publish()` calls it on the\n  whole item right before `put_item`. Because it covers the whole item at the\n  write boundary, it doesn't matter which field a float is in. So a new computed\n  field added later (an average, a ratio, a weight) can't cause this error again.\n  Scores are stored as exact DynamoDB numbers such as `0.4123`.\n- `tests/test_publish.py`: added a regression test that adds one story first and\n  then publishes a second one through `handler()`. It checks that the response\n  is 201 and that the stored score is a non-zero `Decimal`. Also added a unit\n  test for `to_dynamo()` with nested floats. Both new tests fail on the old code\n  and pass with the fix (`python3 -m unittest discover tests`: 3 tests, OK).\n\nWhen adding write-path tests in future, start from a table that already has\ndata. The empty-table path only runs once in production.\n"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MneeMWJFRDXkjXVeojP3Hq","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /private/tmp/h-JsgnfC/ANSWER.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"af5e850f-c4c8-44d5-b4f3-16cd9dbb32b3","uuid":"1405913c-ba4b-4de7-8772-c23bd2f2139f","timestamp":"2026-10-20T23:56:01.003Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"create","filePath":"/private/tmp/h-JsgnfC/ANSWER.md","content":"# Why the second publish returns 500\n\n## Cause\n\n`publish()` stores each story with its three most similar existing stories,\n`similar: [{slug, score}]`. `similarity()` returns `round(0.7 * tag_score + 0.3 * word_score, 4)`,\nwhich is a Python `float`. boto3's DynamoDB serializer rejects floats:\n\n```\nTypeError: Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead.\n```\n\n(`logs/error.log`, raised from `table.put_item(Item=item)` in `src/app.py`.)\n\nThe first publish worked only because the table was empty. `related()` had\nnothing to score, so `similar` was `[]` and the item had no floats in it\n(`similar=0` in the log). From the second publish on there is always at least\none existing story, so a float score ends up in the item and `put_item` throws.\nThe generic `except Exception` in `handler()` turns that into a 500.\n\nThe existing test didn't catch it because it only published into an empty table.\n\n## Fix\n\n- `src/app.py`: added `to_dynamo()`, which goes through the item recursively and\n  replaces every `float` with `Decimal(str(value))`. `publish()` calls it on the\n  whole item right before `put_item`. Because it covers the whole item at the\n  write boundary, it doesn't matter which field a float is in. So a new computed\n  field added later (an average, a ratio, a weight) can't cause this error again.\n  Scores are stored as exact DynamoDB numbers such as `0.4123`.\n- `tests/test_publish.py`: added a regression test that adds one story first and\n  then publishes a second one through `handler()`. It checks that the response\n  is 201 and that the stored score is a non-zero `Decimal`. Also added a unit\n  test for `to_dynamo()` with nested floats. Both new tests fail on the old code\n  and pass with the fix (`python3 -m unittest discover tests`: 3 tests, OK).\n\nWhen adding write-path tests in future, start from a table that already has\ndata. The empty-table path only runs once in production.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01MneeMWJFRDXkjXVeojP3Hq","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEPkqmJfbcMuFPDZioBv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed it and wrote up the cause and fix in `ANSWER.md`. The tests pass, but nothing was published against a real DynamoDB table. Everything was checked against the in-memory fake table in `tests/fake_dynamo.py`.\n\n**Cause:** `similarity()` returns a Python `float` (`round(…, 4)`), and DynamoDB won't accept floats. The first publish ran against an empty table, so there were no related stories to score. `similar` was `[]`, the item contained no floats, and it saved fine. From the second publish on, a float score ends up in the item. `put_item` then raises `TypeError: Float types are not supported`, and the handler returns that as a 500. The existing test only ever published into an empty table, so it never ran the scoring code.\n\n**Fix:**\n- **`src/app.py`:** a new `to_dynamo()` function replaces every float in the item, however deeply nested, with a `Decimal`. `publish()` runs the whole item through it just before `put_item`. Because it works on the whole item, a float can't reach DynamoDB from any field, including ones added later.\n- **`tests/test_publish.py`:** two new tests:\n  - one adds a story first, then publishes a second through `handler()`, and checks for a 201 and a non-zero `Decimal` score;\n  - one checks that `to_dynamo()` converts nested floats.\n\n  Both new tests fail on the old code and pass with the fix (3 tests run, all pass)."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":899,"cache_read_input_tokens":25679,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":899},"output_tokens":482,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"af5e850f-c4c8-44d5-b4f3-16cd9dbb32b3","uuid":"b2602a51-0efb-49e0-87d6-16ad680bcc1d","timestamp":"2026-10-20T23:56:08.662Z","request_id":"req_011CgEPkqUw8Wi4wFMS9kcTE"}
