to score. `similar` was `[]`, the item contained no floats, and it saved fine. From the second publish on, a float score ends up in the item. `put_item` then raises `TypeError: Float types are not supported`, and the handler returns that as a 500. The existing test only ever published into an empty table, so it never ran the scoring code.\n\n**Fix:**\n- **`src/app.py`:** a new `to_dynamo()` function replaces every float in the item, however deeply nested, with a `Decimal`. `publish()` runs the whole item through it just before `put_item`. Because it works on the whole item, a float can't reach DynamoDB from any field, including ones added later.\n- **`tests/test_publish.py`:** two new tests:\n  - one adds a story first, then publishes a second through `handler()`, and checks for a 201 and a non-zero `Decimal` score;\n  - one checks that `to_dynamo()` converts nested floats.\n\n  Both new tests fail on the old code and pass with the fix (3 tests run, all pass).","ttft_ms":3661,"type":"result","duration_ms":40925,"uuid":"6926d0e8-0df7-4898-822c-e4275f1d9d3e","ttft_stream_ms":2654,"time_to_request_ms":190,"first_content_frame_ms":2655,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
